tation","data_points":[{"x":0.0,"y":30.0,"z":0.0}],"uuid":"b336bd83-70c6-5a6c-a66e-b061c635afcb","time":3,"color":-1,"interpolation":"catmullrom"}]}}}],"description":"# ruin_warning\n\nViolet ruin, part 1 (boss area attack): a 20 m ring (radius 356 u) of violet runes on the ground that brightens over 3 seconds.\n\n- Bounds (first set): x -358..358, y 0..1, z -358..358 units (20.14 x 0.02 x 20.14 m). Origin at the base centre, front faces -Z.\n- Texture: 64 x 64, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering; every visible face has its own region painted with its material at world position (identical faces share one). No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: 176.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 716 x 1 x 716 (w x h x d), centred at x 0, z 0\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | what moves |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `warn` | 3.0 | once | runes lift off the ground and turn (0 to 3 s) while the game raises their brightness; at 3.0 s `ruin_column` slams down |\n\n- Glowing cubes (`glow_*`): glow_ring0, glow_ring1, glow_ring10, glow_ring11, glow_ring12, glow_ring13, glow_ring14, glow_ring15, glow_ring16, glow_ring17, glow_ring18, glow_ring19 ...\n\n## Notes\n\n- Bright simple glowing shapes; every lit cube is named `glow_*` (flat colours; the game may scale, spin and fade them). No particles or lights in the file.\n"}